{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:67583",
  "title": "Low: rsyslog security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-09-16 18:04:51"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-09-24 12:14:05"
  },
  "severity": "Low",
  "description": "The rsyslog packages provide an enhanced, multi-threaded syslog daemon. It supports MySQL, syslog/TCP, RFC 3195, permitted sender lists, filtering on any message part, and fine-grained control over output format.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* rsyslog: A configuration-dependent issue in rsyslog's optional imptcp input module can allow an unauthenticated remote peer to crash rsyslogd (CVE-2026-19654)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
